#X obj 230 78 cnv 1 535 191 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -237178 -1 0;
#X text 240 83 The object takes a list of bits (0s and 1s) and produces
bang events for each bit that is set to 1\. In the default mode each
bit is associated with its own outlet \, and a bang is sent to the
outlet corresponding to each 1-bit. If the @rev flag is set \, the
bit order is reversed before processing.;
#X text 240 184 In @poly mode a single outlet is used \, and instead
of a bare bang \, a list (BIT_INDEX bang) is sent — this is convenient
for use with the [clone] object \, where the index identifies the clone
instance.;
